    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="72">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 72</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ þær se bonda sæt uncwydd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_72.lnote.oe.22-2"/> ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wif ⁊ þa cild on þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ylcan unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>And ðær se bunda sæt uncwyd [his deig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_72.lnote.oe.5-2"/>] ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wif ⁊ ða cild unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>And þær se bonda sæt uncwyd ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wif ⁊ þa cild on þam ylcan unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Et ubi bónda (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_72.lnote.oe.22"/> est paterfamilias) mansit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_72.lnote.oe.23"/> sine compellatione et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_72.lnote.oe.24"/> calumpnia, sint uxor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IICn_72.lnote.oe.25"/> et pueri in eodem sine querela.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Ubi homo sine aliqua calumpnia, aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_72.lnote.oe.19"/> de terra aut de alia re, moritur, uxor eius et pueri remaneant similiter.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Uir autem quod uiuens tenuit sine calumpnia, post decessum uiri teneat uxor illius idem et filii sine calumpnia.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="72" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="210" ed="#robertson"/>And ðær se bunda sæt uncwyd [his deig]<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_72.robnote.fn.5"/> ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þæt wif ⁊ ða cild [on þam ylcan]<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_72.robnote.fn.6"/> unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="290" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And þær se bonda sæt uncwydd his deig and unbecrafod, sitte þæt wif and þa cild on þam ylcan unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_72.lnote.de.1"/> wo der freie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_72.lnote.de.2"/> Hausvater unangesprochen und unbeklagt (sein Lebtag <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) gesessen hat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_72.lnote.de.3"/>, auf demselben [Hofe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_72.lnote.de.4"/>] sitze unbestritten die Ehefrau und die Kinder.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And where the free householder has sat unchallenged and unaccused (all his life, B), on that same [homestead] let the wife and the children sit undisputed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_72.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="211" ed="#robertson"/>And when a householder has dwelt all his time free from claims and charges, his wife and children shall dwell [on the same property] unmolested by litigation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_72.whinote.n.1"/><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>And where the householder dwelt undisturbed by charges and claims, the wife and children are to dwell on the same [property] unmolested by litigation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="291" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if a householder has remained free of claims and accusations during his lifetime, his wife and children may afterward hold that same property uncontested.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="359"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III Atr. 14</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 72-72:1: (III Atr 14)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="385"><label>shared formula</label> <ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref> <quote>their formulaic 'æt uncwydd 7 unbecrafod'</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="472"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref> <quote>cf. III Ethelred, 14</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="385"><label>compatible context</label> <ref target="clause:Becwaeth_1">Becwæð</ref> <quote>the tensions over property disposal that inspired laws by Æthelred and Cnut [n. III Atr 14, II Cn 72]</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Atr 14.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 359, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">his deig: omitted GA, added in B in a sixteenth-century hand</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">on þam ylcan: omitted B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quia <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quia Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius added by Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">am Rande im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi> [<hi rend="italic">vgl. III Atr.</hi> 14]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the margin in the 16th cent. [cf. III Atr. 14]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Glosse fehlt Hn</hi> 14, 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gloss lacking in Hn 14, 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">manserit <hi rend="italic">Hk Hn</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">manserit Hk Hn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et c. <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et c. lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. et u. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. et u. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.22-2" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-yd <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-yd Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 14, 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 14, 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Ton liegt nicht auf dem Stande, sondern auf der Grundbesitzer- Eigenschaft des Verstorbenen; in der Quelle stand indefinit ‘jemand’. Der gemeinfreie Bauer ist, wie früher <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi>, nur als der typische Volksgenoss genannt; der Satz soll gewiss ebenso für Thegnas auf Bocland (gegen Lewis <hi rend="italic">Laws of Wales</hi> 277) und Patrizier im Stadthaus gelten. Wenn Inst und zu 72, 1 Q daneben Fahrhabe verstehen, so irren sie</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The emphasis lies not on the rank but on the deceased’s status as a landowner; the source had the indefinite ‘anyone’. The common free peasant is named, like the <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> formerly, only as the typical member of the people; the sentence is certainly meant to apply equally to thegns on bookland (against Lewis <hi rend="italic">Laws of Wales</hi> 277) and to patricians in a town house. If Inst, and Q on 72, 1, understand movables as well, they are mistaken</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Erbnehmer 2—c; Grundbesitz 14</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Erbnehmer 2—c; Grundbesitz 14</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_72.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Adverbialisch ‘ebenfalls’ Inst, Schmid; diese Bed. ‘ebenso’ find ich nur für <hi rend="italic">ilce</hi>.—Wiederum wie <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 70, 1⁴ keine Erbgangsregel!</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Adverbially ‘likewise’ Inst, Schmid; this meaning ‘likewise’ I find only for <hi rend="italic">ilce</hi>.—Again, as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 70, 1⁴, no rule of inheritance!</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_72.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. III Atr. 14; V, 32, 3, and 5 D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_72.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope></bibl><label>deig</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A, Ld; written in the margin in 16th cent. in B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_72.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope></bibl><label>ylcan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">G, A, Ld; om. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_72.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">472</biblScope></bibl><label>72</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">cf. III Ethelred, 14</seg></note>
